Package: sol
Version: @VERSION@
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: sol <noreply@github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), foot, mawk | gawk | original-awk
Recommends: python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, libgtk-layer-shell0, waybar, fuzzel, mako, fonts-jetbrains-mono, xdg-desktop-portal-wlr, xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
Homepage: https://github.com/bachata-dev/sol
Description: your desktop is the solar system, for driftwm
 sol turns driftwm's infinite canvas into a place you already know: the Sun at
 the origin and eight planets in the order everyone learned as a child, each
 sitting where it really was, on its own ellipse, with the Sun at a focus.
 Distance from the Sun is distance from your attention — inner planets are
 immediate, the asteroid belt divides, outer planets are background.
 .
 It gives an infinite plane the one thing it lacks, which is somewhere to be.
 Windows belong to districts, a district tidies into a grid on a card in its
 planet's colour, the bar names where you are, and the whole system is one
 GLSL shader that costs no windows and no meaningful CPU.
 .
 driftwm itself is not packaged for Debian and so cannot be declared as a
 dependency here. Install it from https://github.com/malbiruk/driftwm; `sol
 doctor` will tell you what is missing and what it costs you. The screen
 modes — focus, solo and present — additionally need a driftwm new enough to
 have a Resize in its IPC, and refuse with an explanation on one that does not.
 .
 After installing, run `sol setup` to put the config in your home directory.
 A package installs once for a machine and a config belongs to a person, so
 nothing is written under /home until you ask for it.
